# pjproject's digest authentication copied pre-hashed credential data
# into a fixed stack buffer using the credential's own length field, with
# only a lower-bound check, so an over-long digest string overflowed the
# 128-byte ha1 buffer (stack buffer overflow, CWE-121/CWE-787; PR #4912).
# The pre-computed branch of pjsip_auth_create_digest2 in pjsip/src/
# pjsip/sip_auth_client.c validated
# `PJ_ASSERT_RETURN(cred_info->data.slen >= (pj_ssize_t)digest_strlen,
# PJ_EINVAL)` -- enough bytes, never too many -- and then did
# `pj_memcpy( ha1, cred_info->data.ptr, cred_info->data.slen );` into
# `char ha1[PJSIP_AUTH_MAX_DIGEST_BUFFER_LENGTH * 2]`. The fixing commit
# c82123ea6f ("Fix stack buffer overflow in pjsip_auth_create_digest2()"):
# the copy takes exactly digest_strlen, capping it to the expected digest
# hex length regardless of trailing bytes the caller included.
#
# Detected by the self_sized_declared_array fact
# (ccSelfSizedCopyIntoDeclaredArrayObservations,
# internal/extract/frontend/treesitter/c.go) through binding
# selfSizedCopyDeclaredArray in vyql/bindings/c/
# self_sized_copy_declared_array.vyql, judged by VYQL-MEM-076. The fact
# reports a byte-count copy whose count is the copied object's own length
# field -- source and count reading two fields of one object, here
# cred_info->data.ptr with cred_info->data.slen -- into an array the
# function declares with a constant size, when no relational comparison
# in the function relates that destination's size to anything. The
# declaration is the only statement of the destination's capacity and a
# count taken from the object being copied is bounded by that object,
# not by the destination, so the lower bound does not discharge it: it
# proves the source suffices and says nothing about the array. The fix
# replaces the self-declared count with a separately computed bound, and
# the fact no longer pairs the arguments; the unconditional VYQL-MEM-016
# raw-copy smell fires on both forms, and pj_memcpy itself was unlabelled
# before the binding's alias list named it.
#
# The destination half is what keeps the rule quiet on the 153 same-base
# copies the collateral trees hold: a count read from the copied object
# into a caller-supplied or heap-allocated buffer has no declared
# capacity to consult, so the fourth case rejects. An explicit bound on
# the count against the destination's own size clears it (third case,
# OpenSSL's ssl_session_hash shape), in either operand order.
#
# Measured on the real checkout, 3 x --cache off runs per revision
# (timeout 180, --max-ram 6GB): pjsip/src reports 1067 findings at the
# parent with VYQL-MEM-076 at sip_auth_client.c:385 beside three more on
# the same idiom in sip_auth_aka.c, and 1066 at the fix with the CVE
# site gone -- every other rule count identical across all six runs.
# Collateral: pjlib/src 1 (os_info.c, the same idiom), openssl/test 1,
# mbedtls/programs 1, and 0 across mbedtls/library, httpd/modules,
# hermes/external, ImageMagick6/coders and grpc/src/core; the openssl,
# ImageMagick6 and grpc full trees abort at the 6GB ceiling and are not
# measurable under it.

test "rank1580: the pre-computed digest is copied by the credential's own length"
  lang c
  file pjsip/src/pjsip/sip_auth_client.c
  expect VYQL-MEM-076
  code
  ```
  #include <string.h>

  typedef struct { const char *ptr; long slen; } pj_str_t;
  typedef struct { int data_type; pj_str_t data; } pjsip_cred_info;

  #define pj_memcpy memcpy

  #define PJSIP_CRED_DATA_DIGEST 2
  #define PJSIP_AUTH_MAX_DIGEST_BUFFER_LENGTH 64

  char *create_digest2(char *result, const pjsip_cred_info *cred_info,
                       unsigned digest_strlen)
  {
      char ha1[PJSIP_AUTH_MAX_DIGEST_BUFFER_LENGTH * 2];

      if (result_len(result) < digest_strlen)
          return NULL;

      if (cred_info->data_type == PJSIP_CRED_DATA_DIGEST) {
          if (cred_info->data.slen < digest_strlen)
              return NULL;
          pj_memcpy(ha1, cred_info->data.ptr, cred_info->data.slen);
      }
      return ha1;
  }
  ```

